> does ICU on Windows offer returning the Default UI language and default Region too?

@tarekgh: No, it currently does not. Probably the best way to think about ICU is that it is more like how NLS works (ie: locale data). On Windows, the NLS doesn't provide the Default UI language either, as that is from the MUI APIs, as the setting is owned by MUI.
The region is different though, as NLS does own the region setting and has APIs for it. However, AFAIK, the ICU currently doesn't have any concept of a default "region" for the host OS.
